  "question": {
    "text": "A body takes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>min</mi></math> to cool from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">℃</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">℃</mi></math>. If the temperature of the surroundings is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">℃</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>527</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">℃</mi></math> respectively. The final temperature of the body is"
  },
